index 7a3126a..e5ea117 100644
--- a/docs/business-rules.md
+++ b/docs/business-rules.md
@@ -55,10 +55,32 @@ ### User Roles
 - Owner cannot be removed while being owner; transfer ownership before downgrading or deleting.
 - Only owner accesses billing, plan and payment data.
 
+### Member Invitations
+
+Membership is **invite-only**; managers no longer add existing accounts directly.
+
+- An owner or admin invites an e-mail address with role `admin` or `employee`
+  (`owner` is never invitable — that path is ownership transfer in Settings).
+- Invites expire **7 days** after creation. An invite is pending while not
+  accepted and not expired. E-mails are stored trimmed and lowercase, and only
+  one invite per `(entity, e-mail)` may exist; an expired invite may be replaced.
+- The invitee signs in (or registers) with that address and accepts or declines
+  from the entity switcher or onboarding. Acceptance creates the membership with
+  the invited role, records `accepted_at`, selects the entity tenant and redirects
+  to its dashboard. Declining deletes the invite.
+- Members are managed only by owner/admin: role changes are explicit (save role)
+  and removal requires confirmation. The owner membership is immutable and the
+  last manager can never be demoted or removed.
+- Successful invites are rate limited to **10 per manager per entity per hour**
+  (invalid or rejected attempts do not consume the quota).
+
 ## User Administration
 
 | Action | Who can | Rules |
 | ---- | --------- | ------ |
+| Invite member | Admin, owner (own entity) | Invite an e-mail with `admin`/`employee`; pending invite is unique per entity; owner cannot be invited. |
+| Cancel invite | Admin, owner (own entity) | Deletes a pending invite of that entity. |
+| Accept/decline invite | Invitee (e-mail match) | Acceptance creates the membership with the invited role; decline deletes the invite. |
 | Edit account | Admin, owner (own entity) | Profile data and preferences; respect plan limits. |
 | Reset password | Admin, owner | Reset flow for **account** (login) and **user** (entity member), per security policy. |
 | Remove account | Admin, owner | Not applicable to owner while being owner. |
